  --- did /etc/passwd or the home dir get touched? 
      /etc/passwd mtime: Aug 13 04:51

WHAT THE NAMES BECAME — the R13 claim, measured:
  `id`$(whoami)&&rm -rf ~.pdf   ->  jobs/<id>/output/_id_whoami_rm_-rf_-compressed.pdf
  ....//....//etc/passwd.pdf      ->  jobs/<id>/output/passwd-compressed.pdf
  Every backtick, $(), && and traversal segment is gone. No storage key and no
  path under DATA_DIR contains a quote, an angle bracket, '..' or a backtick.
  /etc/passwd was not touched. R13: PASS, live.

AND ONE NEW FINDING — P2, fixed on this branch:
  A filename containing a raw double quote makes the Content-Disposition
  header ambiguous. undici throws TypeError "Failed to parse body as
  FormData.", which fell through to the submit route's generic catch and
  became HTTP 500 "Unexpected server error while submitting the job." —
  and the server log for that request was EMPTY. A malformed request is the
  caller's error (400), and a 500 that logs nothing cannot be diagnosed.
  Reachability, stated honestly: a spec-conforming client escapes the quote
  as %22 and round-trips fine (asserted in finalPrelaunchRegression R19b),
  so no browser reaches this. The public API does.
  The three Workspace upload routes ALREADY answered 400 "Malformed
  multipart body." for the same input; only the two tool submit paths did
  not. Fixed at both, with the same message, plus a log line at each of the
  two unclassified-500 sites. Mutations U1-U3 in mutation-U-malformed-body.log.
